<section id="adminGuideContent" class="role-guide d-none" data-role-guide="admin" data-guide-description="Projects, deletion approvals and office settings." hidden aria-label="Admin instructions">
<h2 class="role-guide-heading" tabindex="-1">Where to click</h2>
<table class="role-guide-map" aria-label="Admin button locations"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Task</th><th scope="col">Find the control here</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Find a project</th><td><div class="guide-path">Choose a view under <strong class="guide-control">View All Projects</strong></div><small class="guide-location">Left sidebar. Select a project title to open its details.</small></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Add or edit</th><td><div class="guide-path"><strong class="guide-control"><svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg>Add Project</strong> — top right of View All Projects.<span class="guide-path-line">Project title → <strong class="guide-control"><svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m16 3 5 5M4 20l4-1L21 6a2 2 0 0 0-5-3L3 16l-1 5Z"/></svg>Edit</strong> — bottom left of Project Details.</span></div></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Review deletion requests</th><td><div class="guide-path"><strong class="guide-control">Administration → Deletion Requests</strong></div><small class="guide-location">Review first, then Continue to final confirmation.</small></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Import or export</th><td><div class="guide-path"><strong class="guide-control">Import</strong> / <strong class="guide-control">Export</strong> under <strong>File Options</strong></div><small class="guide-location">Above the project table, in View All Projects.</small></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Settings and backups</th><td><div class="guide-path"><strong class="guide-control">Administration</strong> in the left sidebar</div><small class="guide-location">Philippine holidays, Timeline day settings, and Automatic project backups.</small></td></tr></tbody></table>
<p class="role-guide-profile"><strong>Your profile:</strong> top-right avatar → <strong>Edit profile</strong> or <strong>Sign out</strong>.</p><p class="role-guide-phone">On a phone, the navigation menu is at the top.</p>
<div class="role-guide-more"><h3>Extra help, if you need it</h3><details class="role-guide-detail"><summary>Projects, dates, files and printing</summary><div class="role-guide-detail-body"><p><strong>Add:</strong> enter the required project title and approved budget; add known dates and details. Choose Save Project and wait for confirmation. <strong>Edit:</strong> open a project title → Edit at bottom left → Save Changes. Copy important draft changes before reopening a record that another person updated.</p><p><strong>Alerts:</strong> top right of Project Details. Enter actual milestone dates in Edit after work happens. Contract durations and reminders use working days. Contract Due Date is read-only. Record Pre-Inspection before Final Inspection, and Final Inspection before Completion Date. Completion/SWA actual dates cannot be in the future. Deadline-based status updates automatically when records are loaded.</p><p><strong>Files:</strong> Edit → Attachments tab → add/remove → Save Changes. Up to 20 files per upload, 25 MB each. <strong>Print:</strong> bottom left of Project Details; printed summaries are reference copies. <strong>Edit History:</strong> next to the bell in Project Details. You can also open Logs on a project row. Imports and edits are recorded in these permanent Logs; corrections add a new entry.</p><p><strong>Import:</strong> use the template, check dates and duplicates, and review results. The whole import is validated before it is saved together. A failed validation saves no projects. Undo of a completed import that created projects still requires deletion approval. <strong>Export:</strong> uses current filters across all matching pages. Use Archive beside a project to move it to Administration → Historical Archive.</p></div></details><details class="role-guide-detail"><summary>Deletion approval and clearing history</summary><div class="role-guide-detail-body"><p><strong>Delete directly:</strong> select Delete on a project row in View All Projects or Administration → Historical Archive → review records → Continue to final confirmation → tick the checkbox → enter your Admin password → Verify password and delete. This final action removes the selected project, its history and attachments.</p><p><strong>Review Staff requests:</strong> Administration → Deletion Requests → Review request. Check the requester, reason and records. Continue to final confirmation approves and opens the last step; Reject request keeps the records. Go back/close stops before deletion. Approved requests remain Active until finished or withdrawn.</p><p><strong>Accountability:</strong> Administration → Accountability. Each entry has a permanent Log number for reference. Use From and To to find activity by date; log numbers stay the same across filters and pages. Clear history clears the shared visible activity list for administrators. Older activity entries are retained.</p><p>Delete all records is at the bottom of View All Projects under Data Management and also requires review, final confirmation and your Admin password. Delete All is available only to Admin. Archive when records need to remain retrievable.</p></div></details><details class="role-guide-detail"><summary>Admin tools, recovery and your account</summary><div class="role-guide-detail-body"><p><strong>Timeline:</strong> left sidebar → Administration → Timeline day settings → Save timeline days. Use the shared working-day calendar; changes affect reminder lead times.</p><p><strong>Backups:</strong> Administration → Automatic project backups. Choose a server destination using Browse or Use default, then Back up projects now. Check the result and latest backup. Automatic copies require the server scheduler.</p><p>Project backups include deletion approvals, import workflow and general activity. They exclude accounts/passwords, profile photos and settings. Ask IT for a full-system backup and restore test.</p><p><strong>Accounts:</strong> Administration → Account Creation → Create account. Set the role and initial password. Use Permissions to grant Staff project access. To reset a password, choose Set new password and confirm with your own Admin password. <strong>Calendar:</strong> Administration → Philippine holidays → Manage calendar. Set working weekdays, add local holidays or refresh the saved calendar. Your top-right avatar opens Edit profile and Sign out. Admin has a 30-minute inactivity timeout and eight-hour session limit. Sign in with the same account in the same tab to review a recovered draft after a timeout.</p></div></details></div>
</section>
